// To clone a repository : git clone <repo link>
// cd <repo name> // to enter into the repo (change directory)
// To clear the terminal : clear
// List of files in the directory : ls
// Hide the files in the directory : ls -h
// To check the status of the repo : git status

// After modifying the files, we need to add them to the staging area before committing.
// To add a file to the staging area : git add <file name>
// To add all the modified files to the staging area : git add .
// To commit the changes : git commit -m "commit message"

// Local(Laptop) to Remote(Github) : git push origin <branch name>

// To exit from repo : cd ..

// To create new folder : mkdir <folder name>

// Init command
// To create a new git repository : git init
// git init
// git remote add origin <repo link> // to add remote repository
// git remote -v // to check the remote repository
// git branch // to check the current branch
// git branch -M main // to rename the default branch to main
// git push -u origin main // to push the code to the remote repository
// -u means upstream, it sets the default remote and branch for the current branch. 
// So that next time we can simply use git push or git pull without specifying the remote and branch name.

// WORKFLOW
// Create Github repo -> Clone -> Changes -> Add -> Commit -> Push 


// GIT BRANCHES
// Branches are used to create a separate line of development in a project.

// Branch commmands
// To check branch : git branch <branch name>
// To rename a branch : git branch -m <old branch name> <new branch name>
// To switch to a branch : git checkout <branch name>
// To create a new branch : git checkout -b <branch name>
// To delete a branch : git branch -d <branch name>


// MERGING CODE
// Merging is the process of combining the changes from one branch into another branch.

// Way 1
// git diff <branch name> // to check the difference between the branches
// git merge <branch name> // to merge 2 branches

// Way 2
// git pull origin <branch name> // to pull the changes from remote branch to local branch

// rESOLVING mERGE cONFLICTS
// Means 2 branches neh same line mei changes kia 
// Merge conflicts occur when git is unable to automatically merge the changes from two branches.
// Tho hume manually btana hoga ki konsa code rakhna hai aur konsa delete karna hai.


// UNDOING CHANGES
// Case-1: Staged Changes
// git reset <file name> // to unstage the changes
// git reset // to unstage all the changes

// Case-2: Commited Changes(for one commit)
// git log // to check the commit history

// HEAD~1 // to go back to the previous commit
// git reset HEAD~1 // to undo the last commit

// Case-3: Commited Changes(for multiple commits)

// Hash means the unique identifier for each commit.
// git reset <commit hash> // to undo the changes from a specific commit
// git reset --hard <commit hash> // to undo the changes from a specific commit and discard all the changes after that commit

